<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Elevated blood pressure at the first visit, 166/94 mmHg (average of two seated readings), without a previous diagnosis of hypertension; no symptoms; out-of-office confirmation with a week of home readings requested: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Right carotid bruit heard at the first visit in a man with no symptoms of stroke or transient ischemic attack; carotid duplex ultrasound and vascular neurology consultation requested: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Recent release from about six years of incarceration: re-entering community life on parole at 65, establishing primary care with no medical records yet received, a rented room, no earned income, and a public reputation he feels as a burden: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Vascular neurology consultation in two weeks, with carotid duplex ultrasound before it, for a right carotid bruit in a man with high blood pressure: degree of stenosis, medical therapy or revascularization, and surveillance. Guideline: 2024 Guideline for the Primary Prevention of Stroke: A Guideline From the American Heart Association/American Stroke Association (Bushnell C, et al. Stroke 2024;55:e344-e424) (2024); Society for Vascular Surgery clinical practice guidelines for management of extracranial cerebrovascular disease (AbuRahma AF, et al. J Vasc Surg 2022;75(1S):4S-22S) (2021) [S]</item><item>Home blood pressure monitoring twice daily for seven days with a validated upper-arm cuff, to confirm or exclude hypertension before treatment; lower salt, the DASH eating pattern, and daily walking. Guideline: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Hypertension 2025;82:e212-e316) (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension, hyperlipidemia and stroke/TIA monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Baseline tests: basic metabolic panel, HbA1c, lipid panel, urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio, TSH, hemoglobin and ALT, and a resting ECG; re-entry screening with a hepatitis C antibody, an interferon-gamma release assay for latent tuberculosis, an HIV test and a hepatitis B panel; PHQ-9. Guideline: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Hypertension 2025;82:e212-e316) (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension, hyperlipidemia and stroke/TIA monographs (2026); Hepatitis C Virus Infection in Adolescents and Adults: Screening (2020); CDC Recommendations for Hepatitis C Screening Among Adults - United States, 2020 (Schillie S, et al. MMWR Recomm Rep 2020;69(RR-2):1-17) (2020); Latent Tuberculosis Infection in Adults: Screening (2023); Prevention and control of tuberculosis in correctional and detention facilities: recommendations from CDC (MMWR Recomm Rep 2006;55(RR-9):1-44) (2006); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item><item>Re-entry support: a release-of-information request for his prison medical records, a social work referral for housing, Social Security and Medicare enrollment, a low-cost pharmacy plan, and a conversation about shame and reputation, with follow-up of mood at each visit. Guideline: Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>
